---
import Canvas, { height } from '../components/Canvas.astro';
import Symbols from '../components/Symbols.astro';
import { description, github, install, title, url } from '../lib/site';
import '@fontsource-variable/jost';
import '../styles/base.css';
import '../styles/site.css';
const canonical = new URL(url(), Astro.site);
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#EEF0E6" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#262421" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonical} />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content={title} />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href={url('favicon.svg')} />
    <title>{title}</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <Symbols />
    <div class="page" style={`--h:${height}`}>
      <Canvas />
      <svg class="threads" preserveAspectRatio="none" viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><g fill="none" stroke="var(--line)" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"><path d="M96 2 2 30 98 55 2 78 50 96" stroke-width="1.5" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" opacity=".3"/><path d="M0 12 100 22M100 36 0 44M0 62 100 70M100 84 0 90" stroke-width="1" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" opacity=".18"/></g></svg>
<main>
<section id="overview">
  <div class="art-m"><svg viewBox="0 0 1100 830" role="img" aria-label="An abstract composition of lines, circles and triangles that forms the letter K"><use href="#hero-art"/></svg></div>
  <h1 class="sr-only">Kido</h1>
  <div class="b figure" style="--x:880;--y:400;--w:440">
    <p><b>Kido</b> is</p>
    <ul>
      <li>an <b>integrated development environment</b>,</li>
      <li>which takes a <b>terminal-first</b> approach,</li>
      <li>provides a native <b>macOS app</b> <small>(iOS coming soon)</small>,</li>
      <li>and a rich UI for the <b>pi coding agent</b>!</li>
    </ul>
    <button type="button" class="brew" data-copy={install} aria-label="Copy the install command of Kido.app"><code>{install}</code></button>
    <p class="links"><a href={url('docs/')}>Documentation</a><a href={github}>GitHub</a></p>
  </div>
</section>
<section id="ko">
  <div class="b part" style="--x:200;--y:985;--w:450">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 72 72"><rect x="6" y="6" width="60" height="60" fill="var(--red)"/><rect x="24" y="24" width="24" height="24" fill="var(--paper)"/></svg>
    <h2>Terminal multiplexer</h2>
    <p>
    A terminal multiplexer, called <b>ko</b>, runs either locally or on a remote devbox.
    It supervises your running processes and agents.
    It is a <b>replacement for tmux</b>.
    </p>
    <p>
    It uses the <b>HTTP</b> and <b>WebSocket</b> protocols.
    This makes it trivial to build new clients for ko and to expose it over the internet. Just put it behind a reverse proxy and stick your favourite authorization method on it.
    </p>
    <p>Under the hood, ko uses <b>libghostty</b> for interacting with the terminal. This makes it possible to support modern terminal features &mdash; clipboard, images, status reporting and many more!</p>
  </div>
</section>
<section id="kido-app">
  <div class="b part" style="--x:810;--y:1670;--w:450">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 72 72"><circle cx="36" cy="36" r="30" fill="var(--blue)"/><circle cx="36" cy="36" r="12" fill="var(--paper)"/></svg>
    <h2>macOS app</h2>
    <p>
    A native macOS app, <b>Kido.app</b>, works as a client for ko.
    It provides sessions, windows, splits and floating windows.</p>
    <p>
    The <b>sidebar</b> on the left shows an overview of all running processes.
    It can be extended by applications running in panes.
    </p>
    <p>
    Powered by <b>libghostty</b> for the terminal and the display, it provides all the modern terminal features, such as clipboard, images, drag and drop and many more.
    </p>
    <p>
    On top, Kido.app provides <b>webview mode</b>, so programs running in the terminal can render rich UIs.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
<section id="koa">
  <div class="b part" style="--x:200;--y:2250;--w:500">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 72 72"><path d="M36 6 68 66H4Z" fill="var(--yellow)"/><path d="M36 34 47 54H25Z" fill="var(--paper)"/></svg>
    <h2>Agent harness</h2>
    <p>
    A <b>pi</b>-based agent harness, called <b>koa</b>, implements a webview to
    render long agent sessions efficiently and concisely.
    </p>
    <p>
    It also provides <b>subagent</b> and <b>async bash</b> tools, which integrate nicely with the sidebar.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
<section id="remote">
  <div class="b part" style="--x:760;--y:2860;--w:450">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 72 72"><path d="M36 4 68 36 36 68 4 36Z" fill="var(--brown)"/><path d="M36 24 48 36 36 48 24 36Z" fill="var(--paper)"/></svg>
    <h2>Remote ready</h2>
    <p>
    You can run ko <b>remotely</b> and connect using <b>Kido.app</b> or the upcoming <b>iOS</b> client.
    </p>
    <p>
    We provide an example deployment to a DigitalOcean droplet,
    exposed via Caddy &mdash; with <b>HTTP/3 and QUIC</b> for roaming &mdash; and with <b>mTLS</b> authentication.
    </p>
    <p>
    Alternatively, ko can run purely via <b>SSH</b> by forwarding a Unix socket back to a local machine.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="dome">
  <div class="dome-grain"></div>
  <footer class="b" style="--x:150;--y:3580;--w:1140"><a class="wordmark" href={url()} aria-label="Kido home"><svg><use href="#mark"/></svg>kido</a><span>Made in Leipzig, Germany.</span><span class="links"><a href={url('docs/')}>Documentation</a><a href={github}>GitHub</a></span></footer>
</section>
</main>
    </div>
    <script>
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-copy]').forEach((button) => {
        button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(button.dataset.copy);
          button.dataset.copied = '';
          setTimeout(() => delete button.dataset.copied, 1200);
        });
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
